      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Transportation Salaya 8409531615</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>First and foremost, you must provide a <strong>self-attested photocopy of the Registration Certificate (RC)</strong>. This document serves as the primary proof of ownership and identity for the vehicle.</p>
<p>Ensure that the copy is clear, legible, and properly signed by the registered owner to validate its authenticity. The transport agency will cross-reference this information with the physical vehicle to confirm that the details match exactly, including the chassis number and engine number.</p>

<p>Alongside the RC, you must submit the <strong>current Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate</strong>. This certificate confirms that your vehicle meets the required environmental emission standards.</p>
<p>Transporters are legally obligated to check this document to ensure that the vehicle is not contributing to excessive pollution during transit. An expired PUC certificate can lead to immediate rejection of the vehicle for loading, so verify the expiration date well in advance of your scheduled pickup.</p>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Another critical component is the <strong>valid insurance certificate</strong>.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>While your personal insurance policy is necessary for your own coverage, the transporter also requires proof that the vehicle is insured against third-party liabilities and potential damages during the journey.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This ensures that both parties are protected in the event of an accident or unforeseen incident on the highway leading to Salaya.</span></li></ul>

<p>Finally, the entire shipment must be accompanied by an <strong>IBA-approved consignment bilty</strong>. This is the official transport contract that details the sender, receiver, vehicle description, and terms of service.</p>
<p>It acts as the legal receipt and tracking document for your car throughout its journey. Without a properly issued bilty, the transporter cannot legally move the vehicle, and you will have no recourse if the vehicle is lost or damaged.</p>

<p>To mitigate financial risks, it is highly advisable to opt for <strong>100% declared-value marine transit insurance</strong>. Unlike basic third-party coverage, this comprehensive insurance policy protects the full market value of your car against specific transit-related risks such as theft, fire, natural disasters, or heavy damage due to accidents.</p>
<p>Given the long-distance nature of the route to Salaya, having full-value coverage provides peace of mind, ensuring that you are compensated for the actual worth of your vehicle rather than a depreciated amount.</p>

